\label{4-eff} Assume $n=\dim (V)=4$ and $P_{m_0}(V)\geq 2$ for some
positive integer $m_0$. Keep the same notation as in \ref{setup}.
Let $Q_4$ be a nef ${\mathbb Q}$-divisor on $V$ and $Q_4'$ a nef
${\mathbb Q}$-divisor on $X'$. Then
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] $K_{X'}+\lceil{q_4\pi^*(K_X)+Q_4'}\rceil+F$ is an effective divisor for all
rational numbers $q_4> 74m_0+37$;

\item[(2)] $mK_V+\lceil{Q}\rceil$ is effective for all integers $m\geq
75m_0+39.$
\end{itemize}

The sequences $\{u_t\}_{t=4}^n$ and $\{w_t\}_{t=4}^n$ are defined by the following rules:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\widetilde{\lambda}_n=m_0$ and,
for all $i<n$, $\widetilde{\lambda}_i=\lambda_i$;

\item $u_4=75\widetilde{\lambda}_4+37$ and  $w_4=151\widetilde{\lambda}_4+75$;

\item for all $i$, $u_i=\widetilde{\lambda}_i+u_{i-1}(2\widetilde{\lambda}_i+1)$
and $w_i=\widetilde{\lambda}_i+w_{i-1}(2\widetilde{\lambda}_i+1)$.
\end{itemize}
